        "text": "# Infinite Loop\n\nAn **infinite loop**  is a loop that never ends because its condition never becomes false, or it has no condition that can stop it.\n\n**Example:** This while loop will keep executing as long as `count >= 0`. Because `count` only increases, and never goes below `0`, the loop will run forever.\n\n```\nlet count = 0;\nwhile (count >= 0){\n   count++;\n}\n```",
